title: Pick prefabs, layers and messages
intro: Fields that name a prefab, a scene, an input action, a collision layer or a message now list what the project has, flag a name it doesn't, and every list narrows as you type.
project: Platformer | Field Pickers

chapter: Prefabs | The burst a coin leaves behind
select: Coin
say: A coin names other things in the project. Its Effect is the prefab it leaves behind when it's collected.
explain: pick:Pickup.Effect | A list of prefabs | Fields that name a prefab now have a button listing the project's prefabs, like the one by fields that name entities.
say: Type a name with a slip in it, and the field says so.
set: Pickup.Effect = Sparkel
expectflagged: Pickup.Effect = Sparkel
explain: field:Pickup.Effect | Flagged | Shown in yellow, with a warning that the project has no prefab called that.
say: Open the list and type the first letters: only the prefabs that match are left. Click one to use it.
pick: Pickup.Effect = Sparkle
expectvalue: Coin.Pickup.Effect = Sparkle
expectflagged: Pickup.Effect = none

chapter: Layers | Who can collect it
explain: field:Pickup.Layers | Collision layers | Layers lists the collision layers things in the project are on: the player's, the enemies', the sword's.
say: Let the enemies snatch coins too. Picking a layer adds it to the list.
pick: Pickup.Layers = Enemy
expectvalue: Coin.Pickup.Layers = Player, Enemy
say: Picking it again takes it out.
pick: Pickup.Layers = Enemy
expectvalue: Coin.Pickup.Layers = Player

chapter: Messages | A counter and what it counts
select: Score
explain: field:Counter.Message | What it counts | The score counter adds up a message. The coins send Score as they're collected.
set: Counter.Message = Coins
expectflagged: Counter.Message = Coins
explain: field:Counter.Message | Nothing sends it | Nothing in the project sends Coins, so the counter would never count. The field says so.
say: The list shows every message the project sends or listens for, each marked sent or heard.
pick: Counter.Message = Score
expectvalue: Score.Counter.Message = Score
expectflagged: Counter.Message = none
say: No more names that quietly match nothing.
